# Author's Response to Commentaries on: &quot;An Interpretation of Part of Gilbert Gottlieb's Legacy: Developmental Systems Theory Contra Developmental Behavior Genetics&quot;

**Authors:** Molenaar, Peter C. M.

## Abstract
In this article, Peter Molenaar responds to three commentaries (this issue) on his article, &quot;An Interpretation of Part of Gilbert Gottlieb's Legacy: Developmental Systems Theory Contra Developmental Behavior Genetics.&quot; He addresses aspects of relational developmental systems (RDS) mentioned and questions raised in each of the commentaries. [This commentary relates to Molenaar's &quot;An Interpretation of Part of Gilbert Gottlieb's Legacy: Developmental Systems Theory Contra Developmental Behavior Genetics&quot; (EJ1144157) and the following commentaries: &quot;Developmental Systems Theory and the Person-Oriented Approach&quot; (EJ1144417), &quot;When the Stars Align: On the Contributions of Gilbert Gottlieb and Peter C. M. Molenaar to Developmental Science Theory and Method&quot; (EJ1144159), and &quot;Who Are We Talking About? A Discussion of Peter Molenaar's Interpretation of Gottlieb's Legacy&quot; (EJ1144424).]

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1144420

